                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the spirit, attitude or qualities of an entrepreneur; enterprising."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "150dd5ca-06e3-40bf-8138-671b9dbc1644",
                                                "sense_id": "34f36f2e-face-359e-ac35-ba445880e7b3",
                                                "text": "Homer’s entrepreneurial spirit proves altogether overly infectious. Homer gives Barney a pep talk when he encounters him dressed up like a baby handing out fliers (Barney in humiliating costumes=always funny) and it isn’t long until Barney has purchased a truck of his own and set up shop as the Plow King."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acd893b9-4074-4330-89c0-554e83415641",
                                                "sense_id": "34f36f2e-face-359e-ac35-ba445880e7b3",
                                                "text": "It is a canard trotted out by lazy or tendentious journalists that nationalised British Railways lacked entrepreneurial flair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
